// The household's own values for the app target, which the repository does not hold.
//
// A checkout builds with the placeholders below. The owner's Mac puts the real values in
// Local.xcconfig beside this file, which Git ignores (copy Local.xcconfig.example), and
// the release job writes them into its own xcconfig from the testflight environment's
// secrets, refusing a placeholder (scripts/macos/build-ios.sh).
//
// HOUSEHOLD_GATEWAY_HOST is the box's tailnet name, where each phone reaches its
// assistant's gateway. GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID is Google's iOS OAuth client for
// com.siqstack.stewardai, which Connect Google in Settings signs in with: PKCE and no
// secret. It is only the part before `.apps.googleusercontent.com`, digits, a hyphen, then
// lowercase letters and digits. The app adds the ending, its redirect scheme is this part
// after `com.googleusercontent.apps.`, and the gateway's channels.household.googleClientId
// must be the same client, ending included.
HOUSEHOLD_GATEWAY_HOST = household.example.ts.net
GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID = 123456789012-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz012345

#include? "Local.xcconfig"
